{"course": {"id": "s15", "title": "Camday – Cambridge Primary Mathematics — Stage 5", "units": [{"n": 1, "t": "The Number System"}, {"n": 2, "t": "2D Shapes"}, {"n": 3, "t": "Numbers and Sequences"}, {"n": 4, "t": "Averages"}, {"n": 5, "t": "Addition and Subtraction (1)"}, {"n": 6, "t": "3D Shapes"}, {"n": 7, "t": "Fractions, Decimals and Percentages"}, {"n": 8, "t": "Probability"}, {"n": 9, "t": "Addition and Subtraction (2)"}, {"n": 10, "t": "Angles"}, {"n": 11, "t": "Multiplication and Division"}, {"n": 12, "t": "Data"}, {"n": 13, "t": "Ratio and Proportion"}, {"n": 14, "t": "Area and Perimeter"}, {"n": 15, "t": "Multiplying and Dividing Fractions and Decimals"}, {"n": 16, "t": "Time"}, {"n": 17, "t": "Number and the Laws of Arithmetic"}, {"n": 18, "t": "Position and Direction"}]}, "unit": {"n": 18, "stage": 15, "title": "Position and Direction", "strandShort": "Geometry and measure", "blurb": "Reading and plotting coordinates in the first quadrant, finding missing vertices of shapes, and translating points and shapes on a grid.", "strand": "Geometry and measure", "framework": "Cambridge Primary Mathematics (0096), Stage 5", "lesson": true, "subject": "maths", "read": "media/read/m5u18.pdf"}, "objectives": {"O1": {"code": "5Gp.01", "sec": "18.1", "codeNote": "", "t": "Read and plot coordinates in the first quadrant, including vertices of shapes."}, "O2": {"code": "5Gp.02", "sec": "18.2", "codeNote": "", "t": "Translate points and 2D shapes on coordinate grids and describe translations."}}, "sections": [{"id": "18.1", "title": "Coordinates", "objs": ["O1"], "lesson": [{"k": "hook", "t": "Treasure map", "p": ["A treasure map has a grid. The treasure is **5 squares across** and **3 squares up** from the corner.", "How could you write its position in a short, exact way? Think about it before you read on."]}, {"k": "recall", "t": "Number lines", "p": ["Count along from 0."], "qq": {"id": "m5u18s1t01", "type": "num", "prompt": "What number is 4 steps right of 0?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 4, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "4."}}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Coordinates", "p": ["**Coordinates** give a position on a grid as **(x, y)**: go **across** first (x-axis), then **up** (y-axis). The corner (0, 0) is the **origin**."], "fig": {"kind": "coord", "x": [0, 8], "y": [0, 6], "points": [{"x": 5, "y": 3, "l": "T (5, 3)"}, {"x": 2, "y": 4, "l": "A (2, 4)"}]}, "p2": ["Treasure: **(5, 3)**. 'Along the corridor, then up the stairs.'"]}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Vertices of shapes", "p": ["Plot the vertices and join them. A rectangle with vertices (1, 1), (5, 1), (5, 4) has its fourth vertex at **(1, 4)** – same x as (1, 1), same y as (5, 4)."]}, {"k": "try", "t": "Read", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m5u18s1t02", "type": "short", "prompt": "Point A on the grid?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(2, 4)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*2\\s*[,;]\\s*4\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": "(2, 4)."}}, {"k": "method", "t": "How do I read and plot coordinates?", "p": ["Step 1: Start at the origin (0, 0).", "Step 2: Go across to the x-value.", "Step 3: Then go up to the y-value.", "Step 4: Write (x, y) with brackets and a comma."]}, {"k": "example", "t": "Plot", "p": [], "q": "Plot (6, 2).", "steps": [["6 across", ""], ["2 up", ""]], "a": "the point (6, 2)"}, {"k": "example", "t": "On an axis", "p": [], "q": "Where is (0, 5)?", "steps": [["0 across", ""], ["5 up", ""]], "a": "on the y-axis"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Fourth vertex", "p": [], "q": "A square has vertices (2, 1), (5, 1), (5, 4). Fourth?", "steps": [["same x as (2, 1), same y as (5, 4)", ""]], "a": "(2, 4)"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Order matters", "p": [], "q": "(3, 1) and (1, 3) are…", "steps": [["3 across 1 up vs 1 across 3 up", ""]], "a": "different points"}, {"k": "try", "t": "Vertex", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m5u18s1t03", "type": "short", "prompt": "Rectangle (0, 0), (4, 0), (4, 2). Fourth vertex?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(0, 2)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*0\\s*[,;]\\s*2\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": "(0, 2)."}}, {"k": "error", "t": "Swapping x and y", "p": ["Find the first wrong line."], "q": "Point 5 across and 3 up.", "lines": ["(3, 5)"], "bad": 0, "why": "Across comes first: (5, 3).", "fix": [["(5, 3)", ""]], "id": "m5u18s1t04"}, {"k": "mistake", "t": "Going up before across", "p": ["x then y: 'along the corridor, then up the stairs'."]}, {"k": "tip", "t": "Real life", "p": ["Maps, computer screens (pixels) and board games like chess use coordinates."]}, {"k": "summary", "t": "What to remember", "p": ["(x, y): across, then up.", "Origin = (0, 0).", "Order matters.", "Use coordinates to find missing vertices."]}], "video": {"src": null, "offset": 0, "dur": 660, "range": ""}, "stops": [{"id": "18.1-k1", "t": 1, "after": 0, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m5u18s1k01", "type": "short", "prompt": "Before you read on: treasure position?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(5, 3)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*5\\s*[,;]\\s*3\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}}, {"id": "18.1-k2", "t": 2, "after": 4, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m5u18s1k02", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "First number in (x, y) is…", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "across", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "up", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}}, {"id": "18.1-k3", "t": 3, "after": 9, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m5u18s1k03", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "(0, 5) is on the…", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "y-axis", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "x-axis", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}}, {"id": "18.1-k4", "t": 4, "after": 14, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m5u18s1k04", "type": "short", "prompt": "Quick check: square (2, 1), (5, 1), (5, 4). Fourth?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(2, 4)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*2\\s*[,;]\\s*4\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}}], "captions": [], "chapters": [[0, 300]], "req": [{"id": "m5u18s1r01", "type": "short", "prompt": "3 across, 7 up?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(3, 7)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*3\\s*[,;]\\s*7\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u18s1r02", "type": "short", "prompt": "6 across, 0 up?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(6, 0)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*6\\s*[,;]\\s*0\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u18s1r03", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "(4, 1): how far up?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "1", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "4", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}, {"id": "m5u18s1r04", "type": "short", "prompt": "The origin?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(0, 0)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*0\\s*[,;]\\s*0\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u18s1r05", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "(7, 0) is on the…", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "x-axis", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "y-axis", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}, {"id": "m5u18s1r06", "type": "short", "prompt": "Rectangle (1, 2), (6, 2), (6, 5). Fourth?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(1, 5)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*1\\s*[,;]\\s*5\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u18s1r07", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Are (2, 6) and (6, 2) the same point?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "no", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "yes", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}, {"id": "m5u18s1r08", "type": "short", "prompt": "Square (0, 0), (3, 0), (0, 3). Fourth?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(3, 3)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*3\\s*[,;]\\s*3\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}], "prac": [{"id": "m5u18s1p01", "type": "short", "prompt": "Midpoint of (2, 4) and (6, 4)?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(4, 4)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*4\\s*[,;]\\s*4\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u18s1p02", "type": "num", "prompt": "Distance from (1, 3) to (8, 3) in squares?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 7, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u18s1p03", "type": "short", "prompt": "Square (1, 1), (4, 1), (4, 4). Fourth?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(1, 4)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*1\\s*[,;]\\s*4\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u18s1p04", "type": "explain", "prompt": "Explain how to plot (3, 5).", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "rubric": [{"pt": "across 3 first", "kw": ["across|along|x|right"]}, {"pt": "up 5", "kw": ["up|y"]}], "need": 2, "model": "Start at (0, 0), go 3 across, then 5 up.", "hint": "", "reason": "Start at (0, 0), go 3 across, then 5 up."}, {"id": "m5u18s1p05", "type": "num", "prompt": "Side length of the square (1, 1), (4, 1), (4, 4), (1, 4)?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 3, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u18s1p06", "type": "num", "prompt": "Perimeter of rectangle (0, 0), (5, 0), (5, 2), (0, 2)?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 14, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u18s1p07", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Which point is on the line through (0, 3) and (6, 3)?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "(4, 3)", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "(3, 4)", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}, {"id": "m5u18s1p08", "type": "short", "prompt": "A is (2, 2). B is 4 right of A. B?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(6, 2)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*6\\s*[,;]\\s*2\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}], "adv": [{"id": "m5u18s1a01", "type": "short", "prompt": "* Advanced. Parallelogram (0, 0), (4, 0), (5, 2). Fourth vertex to the left?", "diff": "VH", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(1, 2)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*1\\s*[,;]\\s*2\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u18s1a02", "type": "num", "prompt": "* Advanced. Area of rectangle (2, 1), (7, 1), (7, 4), (2, 4)?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 15, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "5 × 3.", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u18s1a03", "type": "explain", "prompt": "* Advanced. Points (1, 1), (3, 3), (5, 5) – what do you notice? Give the next point.", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "rubric": [{"pt": "same x and y / diagonal", "kw": ["same|equal|diagonal|line"]}, {"pt": "(7, 7)", "kw": ["7, ?7"]}], "need": 2, "model": "x = y, they lie on a straight diagonal line; next (7, 7).", "hint": "", "reason": "x = y, they lie on a straight diagonal line; next (7, 7)."}], "more": [{"id": "m5u18s1m01", "type": "short", "prompt": "1 across, 1 up?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(1, 1)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*1\\s*[,;]\\s*1\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u18s1m02", "type": "short", "prompt": "4 across, 2 up?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(4, 2)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*4\\s*[,;]\\s*2\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u18s1m03", "type": "short", "prompt": "0 across, 3 up?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(0, 3)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*0\\s*[,;]\\s*3\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u18s1m04", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "(5, 2): how far across?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "5", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "2", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}, {"id": "m5u18s1m05", "type": "short", "prompt": "8 across, 8 up?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(8, 8)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*8\\s*[,;]\\s*8\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u18s1m06", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Coordinates are written…", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "(x, y)", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "(y, x)", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}], "notes": "v4", "pdf": [{"book": "c5u18", "p0": 2, "p1": 5, "label": "pages 2–5", "title": "Lesson 18.1 notes · Coordinates", "note": "The whole lesson as a document you can print, then Practice on paper with answers at the back.", "look": []}]}, {"id": "18.2", "title": "Translation", "objs": ["O2"], "lesson": [{"k": "hook", "t": "Moving a game piece", "p": ["In a computer game a block slides **3 squares right** and **2 squares down**. It does not turn or flip.", "Where does each corner end up? Think about it before you read on."]}, {"k": "recall", "t": "Coordinates", "p": ["(x, y): across then up."], "qq": {"id": "m5u18s2t01", "type": "short", "prompt": "3 right of (1, 4)?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(4, 4)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*4\\s*[,;]\\s*4\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": "(4, 4)."}}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Translation", "p": ["A **translation** slides a shape. Every point moves the **same distance in the same direction**. The shape stays the same size and the same way round."], "fig": {"kind": "coord", "x": [0, 9], "y": [0, 7], "polys": [{"pts": [[1, 4], [3, 4], [3, 6], [1, 6]], "l": "A"}, {"pts": [[4, 2], [6, 2], [6, 4], [4, 4]], "l": "B"}]}, "p2": ["Square A moves **3 right, 2 down** to square B: (1, 4) → (4, 2)."]}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Translating coordinates", "p": [], "table": {"head": ["Move", "Change", "Example: (2, 5)"], "rows": [["right", "add to x", "3 right → (5, 5)"], ["left", "subtract from x", "1 left → (1, 5)"], ["up", "add to y", "2 up → (2, 7)"], ["down", "subtract from y", "4 down → (2, 1)"]]}}, {"k": "try", "t": "Translate", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m5u18s2t02", "type": "short", "prompt": "Translate (2, 5) 1 right and 3 down.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(3, 2)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*3\\s*[,;]\\s*2\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": "(3, 2)."}}, {"k": "method", "t": "How do I translate a shape?", "p": ["Step 1: Translate one vertex at a time.", "Step 2: Right/left changes x; up/down changes y.", "Step 3: Plot the new vertices and join them.", "Step 4: Check the shape has not turned or changed size."]}, {"k": "example", "t": "A point", "p": [], "q": "(4, 1) moves 2 left, 5 up.", "steps": [["x: 4 − 2 = 2", ""], ["y: 1 + 5 = 6", ""]], "a": "(2, 6)"}, {"k": "example", "t": "A triangle", "p": [], "q": "Triangle (1, 1), (3, 1), (1, 4) moves 4 right.", "steps": [["add 4 to each x", ""]], "a": "(5, 1), (7, 1), (5, 4)"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Describe", "p": [], "q": "(2, 3) moves to (6, 1).", "steps": [["x +4 → 4 right", ""], ["y −2 → 2 down", ""]], "a": "4 right, 2 down"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Is it a translation?", "p": [], "q": "A shape is flipped over a line.", "steps": [["not same way round", ""]], "a": "no – that is a reflection"}, {"k": "try", "t": "Describe", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m5u18s2t03", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "(1, 1) moves to (1, 5). The translation?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "4 up", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "4 right", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}}, {"k": "error", "t": "Adding when moving down", "p": ["Find the first wrong line."], "q": "(3, 6) moves 2 down.", "lines": ["(3, 8)"], "bad": 0, "why": "Down subtracts from y: (3, 4).", "fix": [["(3, 4)", ""]], "id": "m5u18s2t04"}, {"k": "mistake", "t": "Mixing up the direction of change", "p": ["Down → y gets smaller; left → x gets smaller."]}, {"k": "tip", "t": "Real life", "p": ["Animations, video games and tiling patterns (wallpaper, floors) use translations."]}, {"k": "summary", "t": "What to remember", "p": ["Translation = slide; same size, same way round.", "Right +x, left −x, up +y, down −y.", "Translate each vertex."]}], "video": {"src": null, "offset": 0, "dur": 660, "range": ""}, "stops": [{"id": "18.2-k1", "t": 1, "after": 0, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m5u18s2k01", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Before you read on: does the block change size?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "no", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "yes", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}}, {"id": "18.2-k2", "t": 2, "after": 4, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m5u18s2k02", "type": "short", "prompt": "(1, 4) moves 3 right, 2 down?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(4, 2)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*4\\s*[,;]\\s*2\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}}, {"id": "18.2-k3", "t": 3, "after": 9, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m5u18s2k03", "type": "short", "prompt": "(4, 1) moves 2 left, 5 up?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(2, 6)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*2\\s*[,;]\\s*6\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}}, {"id": "18.2-k4", "t": 4, "after": 14, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m5u18s2k04", "type": "short", "prompt": "Quick check: (3, 6) moves 2 down?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(3, 4)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*3\\s*[,;]\\s*4\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}}], "captions": [], "chapters": [[0, 300]], "req": [{"id": "m5u18s2r01", "type": "short", "prompt": "(2, 2) moves 3 right?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(5, 2)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*5\\s*[,;]\\s*2\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u18s2r02", "type": "short", "prompt": "(5, 4) moves 2 left?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["(3, 4)", "/^\\s*\\(?\\s*3\\s*[,;]\\s*4\\s*\\)?\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u18s2r03", "type": "short", "prompt": "(1, 1) moves 4 up?", "diff": "M",